---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../../data.mjs";
import { getProductVisual } from "../../product-images.mjs";
import diagramSource from "../../assets/new-products/poly-mailers-customization-diagram.png";
const diagram = await getProductVisual(diagramSource);
const path = "/guides/logo-artwork-checklist/";
const title = "Logo Artwork Checklist for Custom Packaging";
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: title, author: { "@id": `${site.origin}/#organization` }, publisher: { "@id": `${site.origin}/#organization` }, mainEntityOfPage: `${site.origin}${path}`, image: new URL(diagram.imageFull, site.origin).toString(), datePublished: "2026-10-20", dateModified: "2026-10-27", inLanguage: "en" };
const breadcrumbs = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", itemListElement: [{ "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: site.origin }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Buying Guides", item: `${site.origin}/guides/` }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Logo artwork checklist", item: `${site.origin}${path}` }] };
---
<Layout title={`${title} | Welltroy`} description="Prepare vector logo files, front/back placement, color references and seam clearance for custom packaging. Compare digital proofs with physical sample approval." canonicalPath={path} schemas={[schema, breadcrumbs]} ogImage={diagram.imageFull} ogImageAlt="Poly mailer reference drawing with separate print and sealing areas">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/guides/">Buying Guides</a> / Logo artwork</div><p class="eyebrow">Custom printing guide</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="lead">For a custom packaging artwork review, send an editable logo where available, a visual preview, the product and size, front/back placement, color references and quantity per design. Confirm the final production template and proof before approving printing.</p><p class="muted">By Welltroy · Updated <time datetime="2026-10-27">27 October 2026</time></p><nav class="anchor-links" aria-label="In this guide"><a href="#files">Logo files</a><a href="#specification">Front &amp; back</a><a href="#clearance">Seams &amp; seals</a><a href="#colors">Colors</a><a href="#printing">Print method</a><a href="#proofs">Proof vs sample</a><a href="#approval">Approval</a></nav></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container article-layout"><article class="article-main">
    <p>This checklist covers logo artwork for poly shipping bags and bubble mailers, with additional notes for paper packaging. For a poly mailer, identify the film, opening and adhesive flap when you send the artwork; the bag layout and sealing area determine where the print can go.</p>
    <h2 id="files">Which Logo Files Should I Send for Poly Mailer Printing?</h2>
    <p><strong>Send the original editable vector logo, such as AI or a vector PDF, if available, plus a PDF, PNG or JPG preview.</strong> Include the intended print size, product and material. A PDF may contain only a raster image, so the file extension alone does not prove that the artwork is editable vector art.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Logo artwork file checklist"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Useful to send</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Editable logo</td><td>Original vector artwork, such as AI or an editable PDF, where available</td><td>Allows scale and print preparation without relying on a small screenshot</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Visual reference</td><td>A PDF, PNG or JPG showing the intended appearance and orientation</td><td>Helps check that the editable art matches your approved brand design</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Fonts and images</td><td>Identify fonts and supply or embed linked artwork; ask whether text should be outlined</td><td>Reduces missing-font and missing-image changes when the file is opened</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Color references</td><td>Named brand colors or reference codes, plus a sample if exact matching matters</td><td>Color reproduction depends on substrate and print method; a screen preview is not a physical color standard</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>If you only have a low-resolution image, send it for an initial review and say that an editable master is unavailable. Do not assume it can be enlarged for sharp printing. Ask whether the artwork needs to be redrawn before a print-ready proof can be prepared.</p>
    <p><strong>Can I upload a JPG or PNG?</strong> Yes, as a visual reference for review. Upload acceptance does not make a file print-ready, and changing a file extension does not turn a raster logo into vector artwork. The enquiry form accepts up to three files with a combined size of 10 MB or less; include the logo master, preview and brief where available.</p>
    <h2 id="specification">How Do I Specify Front and Back Printing on a Shipping Bag?</h2>
    <p><strong>Label the front and back panels separately and show the intended orientation, logo size and position on each.</strong> Identify the bag opening, flap or handles so the design is reviewed in the correct direction. Confirm quantity for each size, design and color version.</p>
    <ol><li><strong>Name the product and size.</strong> Include the catalogue model or target dimensions, material and finish. A print area cannot be inferred from the outer bag size alone.</li><li><strong>Describe placement.</strong> Identify front/back, orientation, approximate logo position and whether the art should avoid handles, seams, folds, windows or seals.</li><li><strong>Count the designs and colors.</strong> State quantity per size, design and print-color version. Ask for the printing method and any setup or minimum-order difference for each version.</li><li><strong>Request the exact template.</strong> Confirm printable area, safe area, bleed, color format, white-ink or underprint needs, and file export settings for the approved material and method. Do not use a guessed template.</li></ol>
    <div class="guide-callout"><strong>Material changes the result.</strong> Light artwork on natural kraft paper, fine detail on film and printing near a handle or seal each need a product-specific review. Ask for a proof and, when appearance is critical, a physical sample.</div>
    <h2 id="clearance">How Much Print Clearance Does a Poly Mailer Need Around Seams and Seals?</h2>
    <p><strong>Use the production template for the selected bag and printing method; ask Welltroy to confirm the safe area, printable boundary and any bleed.</strong> There is no single clearance stated here for all films, sizes, handles or closures. Outer bag dimensions do not define the printable area.</p>
    <figure class="artwork-reference"><a href={diagram.imageFull} target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="View the poly mailer print-area reference"><img src={diagram.image} srcset={diagram.imageSrcSet} sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 40px), 760px" width={diagram.imageWidth} height={diagram.imageHeight} alt="Poly mailer reference drawing showing separate front and back printing areas, body dimensions and adhesive sealing zone" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a><figcaption>Welltroy poly mailer customization reference. This drawing is not to scale and is not an approved production template for your order.</figcaption></figure>
    <p>Keep critical text and logos inside the agreed safe area. Ask how folds, seams, handles, windows and the adhesive zone affect placement. For the available poly mailer process, see <a href="/products/poly-mailers/#poly-mailer-printing">screen printing and artwork options</a>.</p>
    <h2 id="colors">How Should I Specify a Brand Color for a Printed Mailer Bag?</h2>
    <p><strong>Send a named color reference or code and identify the material it will be printed on.</strong> Where appearance is critical, agree a physical color reference or printed sample and the acceptable variation. A phone or computer screen is useful for layout review but does not establish the color on the final bag.</p>
    <p>Ask whether the proposed process needs spot-color instructions, a particular color format or an underprint. Confirm the actual film or paper color, finish and print sides before comparing results across products.</p>
    <h2 id="printing">Which Printing Method Should I Request for Poly Mailers?</h2>
    <p><strong>Welltroy mainly uses screen printing for custom poly mailers, starting with simple one- or two-color vector logos and text.</strong> The final method depends on the artwork, film, coverage, quantity and sample route. Send complex, multicolor or full-coverage artwork for a separate review rather than assuming every design uses the same process or minimum quantity.</p>
    <p>For bubble mailer examples, review the <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/#bubble-mailer-cases">LUMIÈRE and VERDANT STUDIO customer cases</a> and <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/#bubble-mailer-printing">bubble mailer printing routes</a>. Their constructions and artwork are confirmed per project.</p>
    <h2 id="example">Example: One Logo Across Two Packaging Formats</h2>
    <p>Suppose a brand is comparing poly mailer P04 (catalogue outer size 28 × 37 + 5 cm) with kraft paper bag KP06-V (catalogue size 25 × 13 × 32 cm). These are size references, not print templates. Send one editable logo and a preview for each intended placement. Ask Welltroy to confirm the usable print area, colors, orientation and production method for each product separately; the same artwork dimensions and ink appearance may not transfer between film and kraft paper.</p>
    <h2 id="proofs">For Custom Mailer Bags, What Does a Digital Proof Confirm Compared with a Physical Sample?</h2>
    <p><strong>A digital proof reviews the artwork layout; a physical sample lets you assess the offered material and print result.</strong> Confirm which specification the sample represents. A complete packing check is a separate step using your actual contents.</p>
    <p class="table-scroll-hint">Swipe the table horizontally to compare approval stages.</p><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Digital proof and physical sample approval comparison"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Review stage</th><th scope="col">Check directly</th><th scope="col">Confirm separately</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Digital proof</th><td>Text, logo version, panel orientation, dimensions and placement</td><td>Physical color, texture and finished fit</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Physical printed sample</th><td>The actual supplied material, print appearance and construction</td><td>Any differences from the intended bulk specification</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Complete packing check</th><td>Insertion, closure and the agreed handling checks with your contents</td><td>Written procedure, acceptance criteria and any changes</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <h2 id="approval">What Should I Approve Before Bulk Production?</h2>
    <p><strong>Approve the final specification and artwork version in writing, with a named approver and date.</strong> Keep the proof, sample reference, quantity per design and matching quotation together. A free initial design draft is the start of the review, not automatic permission to print.</p>
    <ul><li>Check the correct product, size, material, front/back orientation, logo version and spelling.</li><li>Check the dimensions and placement against the supplied production template, including the safe area, folds, seams and closure.</li><li>Confirm colors, whether a physical reference or sample is needed, and what variation is acceptable.</li><li>Confirm the final proof version, quantity for each design, and who on your team can approve production.</li></ul>
    <p>Use the <a href="/guides/custom-mailer-sample-approval/#record">sample approval record</a> to track the final reference. When size, material, artwork or quantity changes, ask for the affected proof or sample checks to be repeated and compare the <a href="/guides/compare-custom-mailer-quotes/">updated quotation on the same scope</a>. For your initial enquiry, use the <a href="/guides/custom-packaging-500-pieces/">custom packaging quote checklist</a>.</p>
    <a class="button" href="/quote/?product=multiple-products#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Send your artwork for review</a>
  </article><aside class="side-card"><p class="eyebrow">Product-specific review</p><h2>Where to Start</h2><div class="guide-options">
    <a href="/products/poly-mailers/"><strong>Poly Mailers</strong><span>Confirm film, print area and seal clearance</span></a>
    <a href="/products/kraft-paper-bags/"><strong>Kraft Paper Bags</strong><span>Confirm paper, handles and color appearance</span></a>
    <a href="/products/custom-paper-hang-tags/"><strong>Custom Paper Hang Tags</strong><span>Confirm both sides, hole position and finish</span></a>
  </div><p>Share the product and quantity with your artwork so the review applies to an actual specification.</p></aside></div></section>
</Layout>
<style>.article-main{min-width:0}.article-main td{min-width:145px;vertical-align:top}.article-main th[scope="row"]{vertical-align:top}.article-main li{margin:0 0 10px}.artwork-reference{margin:28px 0;min-width:0}.artwork-reference img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:12px}.artwork-reference figcaption{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin-top:10px}h2[id]{scroll-margin-top:120px}</style>
